<p>AGAs and big range cookers are a different job altogether, so we've covered them in a separate <a href="{{guide:aga-range-cooker-cleaning}}">AGA and range cooker cleaning guide</a>.</p>
<h2>What makes an oven clean take longer?</h2>
<p>Two ovens of the same size can take very different amounts of time. The main factors are:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Carbon build-up.</strong> An oven that hasn't been cleaned for years has hard, layered carbon that has to be softened and removed gradually. Rushing it risks scratching the enamel.</li>
<li><strong>Door design.</strong> Doors that come apart let us clean between the panes, which takes time but makes a visible difference.</li>
<li><strong>Fan covers and liners.</strong> Removable fan covers and side racks add steps. Catalytic liners need careful handling rather than scrubbing.</li>
<li><strong>Extras.</strong> Hobs, extractors, grill pans and microwaves all add time if you'd like them done in the same visit.</li>
<li><strong>Access.</strong> A clear worktop and floor space in front of the oven lets our cleaner set up quickly.</li>
</ul>
<p>Regular cleaning keeps future visits shorter. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:signs-oven-needs-professional-clean}}">how often to clean your oven</a> explains a sensible routine and the signs it's overdue.</p>
<h2>What happens during a professional oven clean?</h2>
<p>Knowing the steps helps explain where the time goes. A typical visit runs like this:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Setting up.</strong> The floor and nearby worktops are protected, and the oven is checked to make sure it's cold and working.</li>
<li><strong>Removing parts.</strong> Racks, shelf supports, trays and any removable fan cover come out to be soaked in a non-caustic solution while the rest of the work goes on.</li>
<li><strong>Taking the door apart.</strong> Where the design allows, the door is removed and the glass panes are separated for cleaning.</li>
<li><strong>Cleaning the cavity.</strong> Carbon is softened and carefully scraped from the base, sides, roof and back, then the surfaces are wiped and rinsed.</li>
<li><strong>Cleaning the soaked parts.</strong> Racks and trays are scrubbed, rinsed and dried.</li>
<li><strong>Reassembly and checks.</strong> Everything is refitted, the outside of the oven and the controls are wiped down, and the oven is switched on briefly to check it heats as it should.</li>
</ol>
<p>If you'd rather tackle a lightly used oven yourself, our step-by-step guide on <a href="{{guide:how-to-clean-an-oven}}">how to clean an oven at home</a> walks through the bicarbonate of soda method.</p>
<h2>How long after oven cleaning can you use it?</h2>
<p>Because our oven cleaning uses fume-free, non-caustic products, there's no harsh chemical smell to clear. Once the oven is reassembled and dry you can usually cook the same day.</p>
<div class="cc-callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Run the empty oven on a moderate heat for ten minutes or so before the first meal. It drives off any remaining moisture from rinsing.</p></div>
<h2>How to prepare for your oven clean</h2>
<p>A few small things help the visit run smoothly:</p>
<ul>
<li>Don't use the oven for a few hours beforehand so it's completely cold when we arrive.</li>
<li>Take any pans, trays or food out of the oven and the storage drawer underneath.</li>
<li>Clear some worktop space nearby for parts and equipment.</li>
<li>Let us know the make and model when you book, along with any faults such as a loose door or a light that doesn't work.</li>
</ul>
<p>You don't need to stay home for the whole visit. Key holding is available if you'll be out, and our guide to <a href="{{guide:preparing-for-your-first-clean}}">preparing for your first professional clean</a> covers access, pets and parking.</p>
<h2>Oven cleaning as part of a bigger clean</h2>
<p>Ovens are often cleaned alongside other work. When you're moving out, the oven is one of the most time-consuming parts of an <a href="{{service:end-of-tenancy-cleaning}}">end of tenancy clean</a>, and it's built into the time we allow. Our guide on <a href="{{guide:how-long-does-end-of-tenancy-cleaning-take}}">how long an end of tenancy clean takes</a> explains how the whole job is planned, and we regularly carry out <a href="{{local:end-of-tenancy-cleaning-hull}}">end of tenancy cleaning in Hull</a> to letting-agent checklists.</p>
<p>Holiday let owners on the coast, from <a href="{{area:bridlington}}">Bridlington</a> to Withernsea, often book an oven clean between seasons, when there's time for a thorough job rather than a quick wipe on a busy changeover day. It fits neatly alongside regular <a href="{{service:holiday-let-airbnb-cleaning}}">holiday let cleaning</a>.</p>
