		'faqs'        => [
			[ 'How often should you clean your oven?', 'A full clean every three to six months suits most households, with spills wiped up once the oven has cooled. Heavy users should aim for the shorter end of that range.' ],
			[ 'Is it bad to never clean your oven?', 'Built-up grease turns into carbon that smokes, smells and can taint food, and pooled fat can catch fire. It also makes the eventual clean much harder.' ],
			[ 'How often should landlords clean the oven in a rental?', 'At the very least between tenancies, so the new tenant starts with a clean oven that matches the check-in inventory. Holiday lets need more frequent attention because of the number of guests.' ],
			[ 'Why does my oven smoke when I turn it on?', 'Usually because old grease and food residue are burning off. A thorough clean normally stops it; if smoke continues afterwards, have the oven checked by an engineer.' ],
