			[ 'Is hot water extraction the same as steam cleaning?', 'Mostly, yes. Carpet “steam cleaning” usually means hot water extraction, where hot water and cleaning solution are sprayed into the carpet and extracted straight back out. True steam is rarely used on carpets.' ],
			[ 'Which carpet cleaning method is best?', 'For most synthetic and wool carpets, hot water extraction gives the deepest clean. Dry methods suit natural fibres such as sisal and jute, or areas that need to be walked on straight away.' ],
			[ 'Does hot water extraction damage carpets?', 'Not when it’s done properly with suitable products and controlled moisture. Problems such as shrinkage or browning usually come from over-wetting, poor extraction or cleaning unsuitable fibres.' ],
			[ 'Can I walk on my carpet after it’s been cleaned?', 'After hot water extraction you can usually walk on it carefully in clean socks, but keep shoes, pets and furniture off until it’s dry, which normally takes a few hours.' ],
