			[ 'What is the best homemade carpet stain remover?', 'For most fresh stains, a few drops of washing-up liquid in cold water, sometimes with a splash of white vinegar, works well. Dab it on from the outside in, then rinse with plain water and blot dry.' ],
			[ 'Can old carpet stains be removed?', 'Many can be improved or removed with professional hot water extraction and the right spotting products. Some, such as turmeric, bleach marks and old pet urine, may be permanent.' ],
			[ 'Why has the stain come back after cleaning?', 'This is called wicking. If the carpet was over-wetted, residue in the backing or underlay rises back up as it dries. Use less liquid, blot thoroughly and dry the area quickly with good airflow.' ],
			[ 'Does vinegar damage carpet?', 'Diluted white vinegar is safe on most carpets, but test a hidden area first and rinse afterwards. Never mix it with bleach, which gives off harmful fumes.' ],
